{
    "pageid": 1810,
    "title": "Commander",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "A commander is the leader of an army flank. Characters are eligible to lead flanks if they are the ruler, their liege's Marshal , have the minor title also called \"Commander\", or a commander of a hired mercenary company/holy order."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Commander minor title",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Barons can grant the \"Commander\" title to 1 character; counts to 2; dukes to 4; kings to 6 and emperors to 8. Nomads have a -4 penalty to their commander limit; khans can have 2 commanders while Khagans can have 4. Nomads have to upgrade the Baghatur Council building at their nomadic capital in order to increase their commander limit; a fully upgraded Baghatur Council will grant +4 to the commander limit and thus completely offset the initial -4 penalty, allowing nomads to hold the same number of commanders as their non-nomadic equivalents."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Hindu characters must be of the Kshatriya caste before they can become commanders. Women can be commanders if full status of women law passed or if the woman is a Shieldmaiden . Cathar, Messalian, Bogomilist, Mazdaki women, as well as Warrior lodge women, can also be commanders if they share their liege's religion."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Appointing commanders to lead armies",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "When you raise levies, flank leaders are chosen randomly from among your commanders, marshal, and self (if not a child or busy). Flank leaders can be reassigned manually as long as the army is not busy in combat."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Commanders may also be assigned to battalions within the army (in the Reorganise Army view). While their effects will be limited to their battalion, they will be ready to replace Flank commanders if they die, and pose an additional threat to enemy commanders in duels. This option is limited to demesne levies and retinues ."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Courtiers of Holy Orders and Mercenaries may also be assigned as flank leaders if part of their liege's troops are in the army, even if they do not have the commander title. They can also be randomly attached to battalions when you hire their liege. However, they can neither be attached to nor removed from battalions inside a flank manually."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Influence",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Out of battle:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "The leader of the center's skill is used to determine the entire army's attrition (?)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "The leader of the center gets siege events(?)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "The leader with the best siege modifier determines siege speed",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "The leader with the best movement modifier determines movement speed",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "In battle:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "The flank leaders each affect their own flank in battle",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Secondary leaders within the same flank have effects on their own sub units",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Tactics",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "The commander can influence tactics selection via martial skill , culture , and traits ."
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "A high martial skill makes good tactics more likely and bad tactics less likely. The important thresholds here are 8, 12, and 16:",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "martial skill of less than 8 makes a terrible commander; some very harmful \"bad\" tactics become more likely - you are better off with no commander at all.",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "martial of  8-11 makes a decent commander",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "martial of 12-15 makes a good commander",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "martial of 16 or above makes a great commander",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Culture enables some exclusive tactics :",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Arabic culture group enables Desert Ambush",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Altaic culture group enables Retreat and Ambush Tactic",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Tibetan culture group enables Mountain Ambush Tactic",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "North Germanic culture group enables Berserker Charge",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Byzantine culture group enables Embolon Charge Formation",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Scottish culture enables Schiltron Formation",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Italian culture enables Pike Column Advance",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "English or Welsh culture enables Massive Longbow Volley Tactic",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "French , Occitan , Norman , German , or Breton culture enables Couched Lance Charge",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Good/bad Traits allow some good/bad tactics .",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Traits enabling good tactics are:",
                                    "children": [
                                        {
                                            "text": "Inspiring Leader or Defender enables Inspired Defense",
                                            "children": []
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "text": "Brave , Cavalry Leader , or Aggressive Leader enables Heroic Counter-Charge",
                                            "children": []
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "text": "Shrewd , Quick , Genius , or Trickster enables Clever Ambush",
                                            "children": []
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "text": "Possessed , or Inspiring Leader AND Zealous enables Gripped by Religious Fervour",
                                            "children": []
                                        }
                                    ]
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Traits enabling bad tactics are:",
                                    "children": [
                                        {
                                            "text": "Wroth or Aggressive Leader enables Reckless Charge",
                                            "children": []
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "text": "Craven or Organizer enables Timid Advance",
                                            "children": []
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "text": "Lisp or Stutter enables Confused Orders",
                                            "children": []
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "text": "Slothful or Shy enables Hesitant Commander",
                                            "children": []
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "text": "Cruel enables Charging Through Own Skirmishers",
                                            "children": []
                                        }
                                    ]
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Notice that Aggressive Leader uniquely enables both a good AND a bad tactic.",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Combat modifiers",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Commander modifiers are based on character traits and scaled by the commander's Martial skill:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "A beneficial impact is multiplied by (1 + 0.05*commander's martial); this can go arbitrarily high. For instance: x1.5 at 10 martial and x2 at 20 martial.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "A negative impact is multiplied by (1 - 0.05*commander martial), and is completely negated when leader martial is 20 or greater.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Leadership traits",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Characters with the most successful martial education ( Brilliant strategist ) start with a free one leadership trait. Leadership traits can be gained after battles, through the War focus , via a favor event, or from a Chinese strategist. Characters usually do not get events to acquire new leadership traits while they have 2 (or more) of them already."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Some leader traits acquired (like Siege Leader) do not take effect until the game is reloaded. This is a bug."
                },
