        {
            "heading": "Events",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Commanders may be wounded , maimed , made incapable , or killed during battle."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Commanders may be captured when a battle is lost."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Strategies",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Invite skillful commanders from other courts ."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Take advantage of conditional traits . Traits such as Holy warrior , Winter soldier , and terrain expertise are very powerful when triggered."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Improve your kill advantage :"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Offense is increased by Direct leader (center flank only) and Aggressive leader .",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Defense is increased by Patient , Defensive leader , and Unyielding leader .",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Improve your morale advantage by combining a kill advantage with morale multipliers:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Morale offense is increased by Inspiring leader , Cruel , and War elephant leader .",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Morale defense is increased by Inspiring leader and Brave .",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Morale defense is decreased by Craven .",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Save morale-specific advantage for close battles . When you're clearly losing, you should order your army to retreat immediately (by right-clicking a destination). When you're clearly winning, you might prefer to deal less morale damage per kill, so the battle is more decisive and you spend less time chasing the enemy."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Match culture and traits with flank composition : For example, a flank of heavy infantry retinues will benefit from a Heavy infantry leader who can use the North Germanic culture-specific tactic . You may wish to put all your retinues on a single flank (with levies at least defending the other flanks) to maximize the effect."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Let new commanders practice . Let them lead flanks in less important battles while your best commanders are safely at home, or let them lead sub-units. Your fresh commanders can gain brave/craven or patient/wroth, which are each useful in some situations. More importantly, they can gain leadership traits, including:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Terrain specialization appropriate for the location",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Winter soldier if the location is experiencing winter",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Holy warrior if Zealous .",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Give your armies exercise . Contribute to allies ' wars, help neighbors fight off heretic uprisings, raid , or fight raiders . Force realms to become your tributaries , then offer to join their wars."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Maximize commander training . A vassal with 12+ martial and a leadership trait may offer to train your commanders (see favors for details). This event chain starts with the vassal, so having more skilled vassals makes it more likely."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Employ a Chinese strategist . A Chinese strategist who is your courtier or vassal will randomly teach Chinese leadership traits to your commanders. A strategist can be requested for 750 grace, or an existing strategist can be poached by granting a title. This event chain starts with the liege, and can only be made more likely by having a golden-age strategist (identifiable by having two Chinese leadership traits rather than just one)."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Exclusive to Byzantine/Roman Empire",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "With imperial elective succession, commanders are both potential successors to the empire and electors choosing the successor. Also, only characters with a title higher than a baron may become commanders (unless there's not enough counts/dukes/kings in the empire to fill all commander slots). Appointing commanders with skill below 10 (12 for the Marshal) or dismissing commanders with skill at least 12 may reduce the emperor's voting power. It is possible to dismiss a commander if:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "he becomes a councilor (except Advisor)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Incapable (includes becoming bedridden from illness)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "inaccessible (includes seclusion, pilgrimage, kow-tow and other traveling which need a regent for the character).",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Note that distinguished and excellent commanders are both influential electors and popular candidates for the throne, a problem if they are not of your dynasty."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Mutilation : Since mutilation is permanent (barring supernatural interference), the commander will be permanently disqualified for succession, although he can still remain a commander. However, consider only mutilating non-dynasts (e.g. if the emperor decides to employ dynasts as commanders)."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Exclusive to Holy Fury DLC",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
